# Sysmon Installation and Configuration

## Overview

Sysmon (System Monitor) is a Windows system service and device driver developed by Microsoft Sysinternals. It provides detailed system activity monitoring that is not available through the default Windows Event Logs.

Unlike standard Windows logging, Sysmon records rich telemetry such as process creation, network connections, registry modifications, driver loading, file creation, DNS queries, and process access events.

These events are invaluable for threat hunting, malware analysis, digital forensics, and incident response.

---

## Purpose

The goal of installing Sysmon in this lab is to generate detailed endpoint telemetry that will later be collected by Splunk Enterprise and used to detect malicious activity.

