## Integration with Splunk

Sysmon does not send events directly to Splunk.

The event flow is:

Windows Activity

↓

Sysmon Driver

↓

Sysmon Service

↓

Windows Event Log

↓

Splunk Universal Forwarder

↓

Splunk Enterprise

This architecture closely resembles enterprise environments where endpoint telemetry is forwarded to a centralized SIEM.

---

## Troubleshooting

### Issue

Splunk Universal Forwarder was unable to subscribe to the Sysmon channel.

Error:

```
Could not subscribe to the event log channel
ErrorCode=5 (Access Denied)
```

### Resolution

Configured the Splunk Universal Forwarder service to run under the Local System account and restarted the service.

After restarting, Sysmon events were successfully ingested into Splunk.

